name: swadpw
comment: Password file management tool for SWAD
date: 20250419
author: Felix Palmen <felix@palmen-it.de>
version: v%%VERSION%%
license: BSD 2-clause (all rights reserved)
www: https://github.com/Zirias/swad
description:
%%name%% allows to create and edit password files for `swad` to be used with
its `file` credential checker. It uses `bcrypt` password hashes in flavors
`$2b$` or `$2y$`. They are internally the same, `$2b$` is the default of
OpenBSD's bcrypt implementation used by `swad`, while `$2y$` is what Apache
uses.

Files created by %%name%% are fully compatible with Apache's `.htpasswd`
format when the `$2y$` hash flavor is chosen and no real names are given for
users.
.

defgroup: 2

[flag a]
description:
Add a new user to the password file. Fails if the user already exists.
.
default: Edit an existing user, fail if the user doesn't exist.

[flag b]
description: Always use the OpenBSD flavor for `bcrypt` hashes (`$2b$`).
default: Prefer OpenBSD, but leave Apache flavor (`$2y$`) when editing.

[flag c cost]
description:
Set the cost factor for newly created `bcrypt` password hashes. The time
needed to hash a password grows exponentially with this factor. For sensible
password security, a factor of at least `12` is recommended nowadays. Setting
the factor too high will cause significant CPU load for every user login.
.
default: 12
min: 10
max: 255

[flag d]
description:
Delete the given user from the password file. Fails if the user doesn't exist.
.

[flag f file]
optional: 0
description: Path to the password file to edit or create.

[flag h]
group: 1
optional: 0
description: Print a help text and exit.

[flag n name]
description: Set an optional real name %%arg%% for the user added or edited.

[flag s]
description:
Allow reading the password from plain standard input if not connected to a
terminal. This is required to use %%name%% in a pipe.
.
default: Fail when standard input is not a terminal.

[flag V]
group: 0
optional: 0
description: Print version information and exit.

[flag y]
description: Always use the Apache flavor for `bcrypt` hashes (`$2y$`).
default: Prefer OpenBSD (`$2b$`), but leave Apache flavor when editing.

[arg user]
optional: 0
description: The user to add or modify.

